.TH "ODIR" "8" "" "Onesimus @VERSION@" "Onesimus"
.SH NAME
odir \- Onesimus Director, a drop\-in replacement for the Bareos Director
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B odir
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B odir
schedules and runs backup, restore, copy, migration and verify jobs, keeps
the catalog and serves the consoles. It reads the Bareos Director
configuration (bareos\-dir.d), speaks the Bareos protocols to File and
Storage Daemons and consoles (bconsole, oconsole) and adds a TLS gRPC
interface (DirectorApi) on the Director port + 1000.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Write the log to
.I path
as well (default
.IR /var/log/onesimus/odir.log );
.B none
for no log file. Without the right to open it odir warns and logs to
stderr only. Colour codes are written only when the log goes to a terminal
alone.
.TP
.BI \-c " path" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " path
Configuration file or directory. Default: /etc/bareos/bareos\-dir.d.
.TP
.BI \-d " level" "\fR, \fP\-\-debug\-level " level
Debug level (999 prints the levels).
.TP
.B \-\-dt
Timestamps in debug output.
.TP
.B \-f\fR, \fP\-\-foreground
Run in the foreground.
.TP
.BI \-u " user" "\fR, \fP\-\-user " user
Run as this user (started as root).
.TP
.BI \-g " group" "\fR, \fP\-\-group " group
Run as this group (started as root).
.TP
.B \-t\fR, \fP\-\-test\-config
Read the configuration, check the resources and the catalog connection,
print the problems and exit (exit status 42 on configuration errors), like
bareos\-dir \-t.
.TP
.B \-k\fR, \fP\-\-kill
Stop the running Director and exit.
.TP
.BI \-p " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-pid\-file " file
PID file.
.TP
.B \-s\fR, \fP\-\-no\-signals
No signal handling (debugging).
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fP\-\-verbose
Verbose messages.
.TP
.BR \-\-xc " [\fIresource\fR]"
Print the configuration, or one resource, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-xs
Print the configuration schema as JSON and exit.
.TP
.BI \-P " port" "\fR, \fP\-\-port " port
Listening port (default from the configuration, usually 9101).
.TP
.BI \-b " address" "\fR, \fP\-\-bind\-address " address
Listen on this address only.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Director name (default from the configuration).
.TP
.BI \-w " dir" "\fR, \fP\-\-working\-directory " dir
Working directory (default /var/lib/bareos).
.TP
.B \-r\fR, \fP\-\-restore\-only
Accept restore jobs only.
.TP
.BI \-m " n" "\fR, \fP\-\-max\-jobs " n
Override the maximum number of concurrent jobs.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-cert " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-tls\-key " file "\fR, \fP\-\-tls\-ca " file
TLS certificate, key and CA (PEM) for the Bareos protocols.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-grpc
Do not start the gRPC server.
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-port " port"
gRPC port (default: Director port + 1000).
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-cert " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-grpc\-key " file
PEM certificate and key for gRPC (default: generated in the working
directory).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
The configuration is the Bareos Director configuration: one directory
bareos\-dir.d with a subdirectory per resource type (director, catalog,
client, job, jobdefs, fileset, schedule, pool, storage, messages, console,
profile, user, counter) and one resource per file. Onesimus directives the
original does not know (GrpcPort, GrpcTlsCertificate, GrpcTlsKey,
MdnsAdvertise, DbDriver) are accepted.
.B configure
and
.B .config
write resources there and reload.
.SH CATALOG
.PP
The catalog is the Bareos PostgreSQL catalog. At start the Director
applies its schema extension in the schema
.B onesimus
(catalog ACLs, journal, helper views and functions); the Bareos tables stay
unchanged.
.SH SYSTEMD
.PP
The package installs
.B odir.service
(user bareos,
.BR "odir \-c /etc/bareos/bareos\-dir.d \-f" ).
.B systemctl reload odir
sends SIGHUP, which reloads the configuration like the console command
.BR reload .
.SH CONSOLE COMMANDS
.PP
Every command has its page
.BR odir\-\fIcommand\fR (7)
(dot commands:
.BR odir\-dot\-\fIname\fR (7));
all are in
.BR odir\-commands (7).
.\" @COMMANDS@
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/onesimus/odir.log
Log file (option
.BR \-\-log\-file ;
rotated by
.IR /etc/logrotate.d/onesimus\-odir ).
.TP
.I /etc/bareos/bareos\-dir.d
Configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bareos
Working directory (state files, gRPC certificate).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bareos/scripts/ddl
Catalog schema files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir\-commands (7),
.BR oconsole (1),
.BR ofd (8),
.BR bareos\-dir (8)
